        "blast_url": "https://blast.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/Blast.cgi?PAGE_TYPE=BlastSearch&PROG_DEF=blastn&BLAST_SPEC=GDH_GCA_988265175.1",
        "comments": "The assembly daPilAura1.hap1.1 is based on 57x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and plastid genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. The species looks to be tetraploid (4n = 36). A translocation was observed between Chromosome 1 and Chromosome 14 and among Chromosome 1 and Chromosomes 6 and 7. The two chromosome-level halotypes are represented in HAP1 file and the other two scaffold-level ones are in HAP2 file.",
